<title>UK: Kvaerner unit wins $49 mln building deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner unit wins $49 mln building deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian engineering and construction group Kvaerner ASA said on Tuesday that its 50-percent owned Hong Kong unit Gammon Construction Ltd had been awarded a $49 million building contract by Ka Chee Co Ltd.  </p>
<p>The contract is to build a commercial office tower --  the Olympia Plaza -- on the site of the demolished Olympia Theatre in Hong Kong, Kvaerner said in a statement.</p>
<p>The 25-storey building will constructed above a three-level car park and comprise a shopping arcade on the three podium levels, restaurants on the middle eight levels and office space on the top 14 floors.</p>
<p>The development is scheduled to be completed in December 1998.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
